{
  "format": "kshader",
  "generator": "Kekenik Shader",
  "graph": {
    "comments": [
      {
        "color": "#60a5fa",
        "id": "note_inputs",
        "position": {
          "x": 22,
          "y": 34
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 39,
          "w": 542
        },
        "text": "Quad UV, time and the particle colour / alpha."
      },
      {
        "color": "#22d3ee",
        "id": "note_noise",
        "position": {
          "x": 768,
          "y": 34
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 39,
          "w": 2598
        },
        "text": "`step = floor(time × rate)` re-seeds the noise: the bolt jumps to a new shape every `1 / rate` s. Signed 1-D value noise along x (`p = (x, ½)`, scale = jag frequency) gives the bend; a second noise at 2.3× frequency adds fine kinks to the branch. The envelope `√(4·x·(1−x))` pins both ends of the bolt to the centre line."
      },
      {
        "color": "#4ade80",
        "id": "note_lines",
        "position": {
          "x": 3570,
          "y": 34
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 39,
          "w": 2072
        },
        "text": "`yc = uv.y − ½`; the distance to a bolt is `|yc − displacement|`. Core = `1 − smoothstep(0, width, dist)`; glow = `saturate(1 − dist / glowWidth)²`. The branch uses the second displacement and half the core width."
      },
      {
        "color": "#fbbf24",
        "id": "note_flash",
        "position": {
          "x": 3570,
          "y": 939
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 39,
          "w": 2072
        },
        "text": "`brightness = lerp(1, hash(step), flicker) × (0.35 + 0.65 × (1 − saw)^decay)`. The sawtooth (period = *Strike Period*) restarts a bright flash that decays; the per-step hash flickers it. `endFade` softens the two bolt ends."
      },
      {
        "color": "#fb923c",
        "id": "note_color",
        "position": {
          "x": 5846,
          "y": 34
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 39,
          "w": 2684
        },
        "text": "`core = core₁ + branch × core₂`, `glow` likewise. Colour = (`coreColor × core + glowColor × glow × strength`) × brightness × endFade × particle colour; alpha = saturate(core + glow) × endFade × particle alpha."
      },
      {
        "color": "#a78bfa",
        "id": "note_out",
        "position": {
          "x": 8734,
          "y": 34
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 39,
          "w": 300
        },
        "text": "Additive blend, ZWrite off, two-sided."
      }
    ],
